course: dictionary
lesson: 10788
title: Valves: little doors for flow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A valve is a part that opens and closes to control how a liquid or gas flows through a pipe or tube. Think of it as a little door that decides when things can pass.
explain: Your heart has valves that let blood flow only one way. «The beat sounds like lub-dub: that is little doors, the valves, snapping shut so the blood can only go one way.» The word «valves» in that sentence is the clue: they are doors that open and shut.
explain: Valves are all around you. A tyre valve lets air in when you pump, and keeps it from leaking out. Taps work like valves too. On a trumpet, valves are buttons that change the note.
fact: A valve opens and closes to control how a liquid or gas flows.
fact: «Valve» means a part that controls flow, not the whole pipe.
fact: «Valves» in the heart let blood flow only one way.
fact: «Lub-dub» is the sound of the heart's valves snapping shut.
fact: A tyre valve lets air in and keeps it from escaping.
exercise: «When you flush, a valve opens and water rushes into the bowl.» What does valve mean? | A bucket for water | A pipe that is always open | A loud noise | *A part that opens and closes to control flow
exercise: «The lub-dub sound is the heart's valves snapping shut.» What do heart valves do? | They make the heart beat faster | They store blood for later | *They let blood flow only one way | They pump air into the lungs
exercise: On a trumpet, what do the valves do? | They hold the mouthpiece in place | They make the trumpet louder when you blow harder | *They change the note | They clean the air as you play
test: What is a tyre valve for? | Holding the wheel on the car | Stopping the car from moving | Making the tyre smell nice | *Letting air in while keeping it from leaking out
test: Why do heart valves matter? | *So blood can only flow one way | So the heart can make a sound like a song | So the lungs can store air | So the heart beats faster
exam: Pupil asks, «Is a valve only found in the heart?» What is the answer? | *Yes, valves are only found in the heart | No, valves also control flow in pipes, taps and tyres | No, valves are only found in trumpets | Yes, but only in old computers
